# LISP recipes

Atomic, ready-to-paste snippets. Prefer these over rolling your own.

## R01 — Load Sylfaen text style

```
(command "_.-STYLE" "GEO" "Sylfaen.ttf" "0" "1" "0" "N" "N" "N")
```

For BPG family (fallback):

```
(command "_.-STYLE" "GEO" "BPGExcelsiorCaps.ttf" "0" "1" "0" "N" "N" "N")
```

## R02 — Set drawing units to mm

```
(setvar "INSUNITS" 4)         ; 4 = mm
(setvar "MEASUREMENT" 1)      ; metric
(setvar "LUNITS" 2)           ; decimal
(setvar "AUNITS" 0)           ; degrees
```

## R03 — Create the standard 11-layer set

```
(defun mk-layer (name color)
  (command "_.-LAYER" "_M" name "_C" color "" ""))

(mk-layer "WALL"        "7")
(mk-layer "WALL-INNER"  "8")
(mk-layer "DOOR"        "4")
(mk-layer "WINDOW"      "5")
(mk-layer "FURN"        "3")
(mk-layer "FIX"         "6")
(mk-layer "GRID"        "1")
(mk-layer "AXIS-LABEL"  "1")
(mk-layer "DIM"         "2")
(mk-layer "TEXT"        "7")
(mk-layer "TITLE"       "7")
```

## R04 — Attach an xref by absolute path

```
(command "_.-XATTACH" "C:/path/to/xref_topo.dwg" "0,0,0" "1" "1" "0")
```

## R05 — Insert MText with Georgian inline override

```
(defun ge (s) (strcat "\\fSylfaen|b0|i0;" s))
(command "_.-MTEXT" "0,0" "0,3000" (ge "ფუნდამენტის გეგმა"))
```

## R06 — Compute the area of a closed LWPOLYLINE

```
(defun poly-area (e / o) (vlax-curve-getarea (vlax-ename->vla-object e)))
```

## R07 — Iterate every entity in modelspace (`ssget X`)

```
(setq ss (ssget "_X"))
(repeat (sslength ss)
  (setq e (ssname ss 0))
  (setq ed (entget e))
  ;; ... do work ...
  (setq ss (ssdel e ss)))
```

## R08 — Filter by type and/or layer

```
(ssget "_X" '((0 . "LWPOLYLINE") (8 . "WALL")))
(ssget "_X" '((0 . "INSERT")    (2 . "Kitchen Layout 26")))
(ssget "_X" '((0 . "DIMENSION")))
```

## R09 — Get bounding box of an entity (vla)

```
(defun bb (e / o lo hi)
  (setq o (vlax-ename->vla-object e))
  (setq lo (vlax-3d-point '(0 0 0)) hi (vlax-3d-point '(0 0 0)))
  (vla-getboundingbox o 'lo 'hi)
  (list (vlax-safearray->list (vlax-variant-value lo))
        (vlax-safearray->list (vlax-variant-value hi))))
```

## R10 — Write JSON to a file

```
(setq fp (open "C:/Users/PCZONE.GE/autocad-mcp/out.json" "w"))
(write-line (strcat "{\"key\":" (rtos value 2 3) "}") fp)
(close fp)
```

> Always use forward slashes in paths from LISP.
> Always quote strings with `\"` inside `strcat`.

