## R12 — Save the active drawing

```
(command "_.QSAVE")
;; or save under new name:
(command "_.SAVEAS" "2018" "C:/path/file.dwg")
```

## R13 — Insert a block at a point

```
(command "_.-INSERT" "BlockName" "100,200" "1" "1" "0")
```

## R14 — Create a closed rectangular polyline

```
(defun rect (x1 y1 x2 y2 layer)
  (command "_.-LAYER" "_S" layer "")
  (command "_.PLINE"
           (list x1 y1) (list x2 y1) (list x2 y2) (list x1 y2) "_C"))
```

## R15 — Batch zoom-extents + plot to PDF

```
(command "_.ZOOM" "_E")
(command "_.-PLOT" "_Y" "_Layout1" "DWG To PDF.pc3" "ANSI A (8.50 x 11.00 Inches)"
         "_M" "_L" "_N" "_E" "1=1" "_C" "_Y" "monochrome.ctb" "_Y" "_N"
         "C:/path/out.pdf" "_N" "_Y")
```

## R16 — One-line dimension creator (DIMLINEAR)

```
(command "_.DIMLINEAR" "100,100" "5600,100" "100,-1500")
```

## R17 — Linear LFAC trick for georeferenced models

When the drawing is in mm but dimensions should display in metres,
set `DIMLFAC = 0.001` once per Dim style:

```
(setvar "DIMLFAC" 0.001)
```

